From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] [Transform] Preserve vector widths for scalar condition
 casts

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Upstream-commit: 71a7c3114e78062a06c0866ef23399cf7aa3f857

Rationale: VectorSizePlanner and DecoupleTypeCast previously inspected casts inside scalar IfThenElse/Select/if_then_else conditions (and scalar Bind values used only in conditions), allowing a narrow dtype cast inside a branch predicate to shrink the loop vector width or trigger unnecessary temporary buffer decoupling. Ignore condition-only scalar casts when planning vectorization and decoupling type casts.

Quality: Improves vectorization width preservation on conditional elementwise loops without altering numerical results or existing spark-ds41f:1107 kernel codegen.

Tests: testing/python/transform/test_tilelang_transform_decouple_type_cast.py and testing/python/transform/test_tilelang_transform_loop_vectorize.py across two GPU boots on SM121.

Upstream-status: Backported from tile-ai/tilelang#3759 (commit 71a7c3114e78062a06c0866ef23399cf7aa3f857).
